      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Osteoporotic vertebral compression fractures are an increasingly common source of morbidity and mortality in the aging population. Previously, these fractures were assumed to be benign, self-limited entities with few, if any, significant sequelae. More recently, however, individual cohorts and population-wide analyses demonstrate high rates of chronic pain, functional decline, physiologic disorder, psychosocial dysfunction, and early mortality among patients with osteoporotic vertebral body compression fractures."},
